For accessing our partitions and subvolumes, we now need to mount them. These
are the different partitions/subvolumes that will be mounted as well as their
respective mountpoints (non-existing mountpoints will be created dynamically):
    - @ subvolume: /mnt
    - @home subvolume: /mnt/home
    - @snp subvolume: /mnt/snp
    - EFI system partition: /mnt/boot

While the @snp subvolume has no use for installing ArchLinux, mounting it now
means that the genfstab script will be able to pick it up and write its
mountpoint to /etc/fstab. This way, the subvolume will be mounted by default on
system boot.
